From 226163c4cfa9c5564b800e1192178ecb8cf6f697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DaffyDabz <daffydabz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:44:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 329/371] pirates: the shipwright's Upgrade does something for
 every ship again, and Sell and Repair work after a sail (boats-0001, client
 only)

The host: the ship Upgrade button does nothing. A ship a pirate sailed and walked off is 'PutAway' until the next login
(DistributedShipAI._playerDeparted), but the shipwright's ship picker (ShipFrameShopping.enableStatsOV) and its sell /
trade-up / overhaul checks (DistributedShopKeeper) only took 'Off', so after any sail the ship's button stayed grey and
the press did nothing. The server (_upgradeShip) already takes 'Off', 'PutAway' and 'Sunk'.

- ShipFrameShopping.SHIP_PUT_AWAY_STATES = ('Off', 'PutAway', 'Sunk'), used by the picker and the three
  DistributedShopKeeper checks.
- The menu's Upgrade is lit for any pirate with a ship (DistributedNPCTownfolk.computeOptions), and the picker's
  Upgrade is always pressable: confirmUpgradeShip asks Yes/No or says why not (put the ship away first, already the
  biggest, Sailing level, gold).

Client only: no server file changes, no restart; shipped as client patch 37. Test: test_upgrade_button.py live FAIL
7/16, patched PASS 16/16.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
